# Fixed defect 132, 2026-09-29, beside it: a line left open over a tabbed
# line. Symptom: `function` alone over a line whose margin holds a tab cost
# `tab_in_indentation` and then `expected_params` at the `=` of the line below,
# whose `y` the head had taken for its name; and `x = a +` over a tabbed `b`
# went on into it with no word said of the break. Cause: where a tab leaves
# the margin unread the lexer let a line left open go on in silence into the
# next one. It ends it there, and the parser says what it lacks: the name,
# and the operand, each once, and the tabbed line is still read, its own `)`
# reported (`selfhost/open_line.hero`, `abandon`).

#~v expected_name
function
    y = 3 )  #~ tab_in_indentation expected_end_of_line

function main()
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    x = 1 +
    print(2)  #~ tab_in_indentation
    print(x)

# Read again 2026-10-01, lane recovery-b5 (ruling 5, `selfhost/indent_runs.hero`):
# a tabbed line is laid out at the margin its fix writes, a tab as four
# columns, so a line left open over it goes on, or is ended, as over that
# margin, and `open_line.abandon` is gone. `function` over a tabbed `y = 3 )`
# is still told its name; `x = 1 +` over a tabbed `print(2)` at its own
# margin is the break panel 181 refuses there, `continuation_outside_brackets`,
# as with spaces, where the line was ended before and the operand named
# missing. Both tabs are certain fixes, which `check --apply` writes
# (`.applied`).
